From 3187b424df0515722487982488048e47943429d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:09:25 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] dpp: recover 1905 security for pre-shared wireless bSTA,
 harden DPP flows

A wireless bSTA that associates to its backhaul BSS using a pre-shared
credential (SAE/PSK) instead of completing a DPP wireless exchange has
no 1905 connector. Add AgentDB::dpp_wireless_recovery_needed() to detect
this and fall back to the wired-style DPP Auth/GAS exchange over the
already-up backhaul link, without disturbing the live association.

Also:
- Simplify reset_1905_security_for_connection_switch() to a single
  parameterless reset on any wired<->wireless switch, and clear
  dpp_credentials_restored so WPA_ATTACH can restore persisted
  connectors again after the switch.
- Scope is_bsta_connected() per radio and gate maybe_start_dpp_chirp()/
  handle_dpp_chirp_timeout() on the actual backhaul connection type
  instead of global FSM state, avoiding spurious chirps for MLO radios.
- Detect and retry a stalled 1905 4-way handshake (PMK derived, TK never
  installed) in DppAgentTask::work(), and drop stale peer_1905_security
  state before a fresh Peer Discovery.
- Register the GW's own LAN switch for DPP-onboarded gateways so WSC
  Ethernet agents can still join.
- Cache signed DPP Connectors in DppKeyStore and reuse the enrollee's
  netAccessKey across reconfigurations so hostapd's dpp_connector=
  stays stable and backhaul STAs aren't dropped on reload.

Signed-off-by: Parimalarengan Gururajan <gururaja@qti.qualcomm.com>
